# Medicine POS Backend

Multi-tenant pharmacy POS for Bangladesh. Rust: axum, SeaORM over PostgreSQL with row-level
security, Redis.

**Read `specs/CONSTITUTION.md` (~1,400 tokens) before your first edit.** It is the only
rulebook; this file restates none of it. Status is `specs/INDEX.md`, or `cargo xtask status`.

**A task is ticked on a command that exits 0, never on intent.** Enforced on every compile by
`crates/server/build.rs` and at commit time by `.githooks/pre-commit`.

**Never open `PRODUCT_SPEC.md` or fetch Notion to check one decision** — ~33,000 tokens for
one line. Use `cargo xtask d 73`, which costs about 40.

```bash
cargo xtask verify --lint        # structural, executes nothing
cargo xtask verify --module 07   # run one module's assertions
cargo xtask d <number|text>      # look up a decision
cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
```

Rules tagged `[CLAUDE]` do not bind you — use the `[ALL]` equivalent stated alongside each.
In particular: run Gate 5 as a separate invocation that did not implement the tasks, and
never write against a crate API from recall — check `Cargo.toml` and read `cargo doc`.
